Subject: build raw URLs for the configured forge in the behaviour harness

The URL-dispatch and base-dispatch steps host a harness in a repository of
the pool organization and point the slot at it by URL. They build that URL,
and the allowed_remote_resources prefix that admits it, for
raw.githubusercontent.com only. Against an enterprise server or an emulator
the slot then names a host the forge is not on, the harness's own
unauthenticated reachability check fails ("raw URL ... not accessible"), and
all six scenarios stop there.

The CLI under test already reads the appliance form when GITHUB_SERVER_URL
names the forge (patch 0007):

  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{owner}/{repo}/{ref}/{path}
  https://{host}/{owner}/{repo}/raw/{ref}/{path}

The two steps now build the second form, and a {server}/{owner}/{repo}/
prefix, when GITHUB_SERVER_URL names a forge other than github.com; on
github.com, or with the variable unset, nothing changes.

Gap BT-H5 of .ledger/plans/fullsend-behaviour-tests-plan.md.

Breadboard note: test-only, like 0017; applied by the behaviour-test run
(deploy/fullsend/behaviour/run.sh), not by deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh.

